1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,420
Taking away on one rod is super quick — check out these examples!

2
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:07,140
Three beads are up.

3
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:10,580
Pull two down — three take away two is one!

4
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:13,320
Let's try another!

5
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:17,220
Two lower beads, plus the upper bead — that's seven.

6
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:21,580
Lift the upper bead — seven take away five is two!

7
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:24,100
Next one!

8
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:28,360
Four lower beads, plus the upper bead — that's nine.

9
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:34,960
Pull one lower bead down, and lift the upper bead — nine take away six is three!

10
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:37,260
One more!

11
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:41,260
Three lower beads, plus the upper bead — that's eight.

12
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:47,880
Pull two lower beads down, and lift the upper bead — eight take away seven is one!

13
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:54,840
Here's one tip: lower beads always move first, then the upper bead!

14
00:00:55,880 --> 00:01:00,340
Lower beads or the upper bead — taking away is always quick!

15
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:05,620
Learn it all with Abacus Kids — free on the App Store and Google Play!
